WEBVTT

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:23.800
<i>Everyday I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:31.140
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:38.880
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:44.950
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.730
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:57.500
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:04.480
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:12.410
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:20.080
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.320
All right...

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.450
Roar!

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:42.220
Get lost, you
big monster!

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.920
Hey! Maho, what are you
doing with that book?

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.930
We're playing monsters
today.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.440
I want to read
my book.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.870
Then we'll play
by ourselves.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.370
Okay.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.810
All right!

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.950
Where should we go
and read, Chibi?

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.310
Wait! Roar!

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.920
I'm gonna eat you!

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.890
You can't catch me! I'm
the Gold Monster King!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.690
No, don't be him!

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:13.660
When the Prince arrived at the
castle, it was very quiet...

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.800
"Sleeping Beauty"
When the Prince arrived at the
castle, it was very quiet...

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:17.870
"Sleeping Beauty"

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.960
...and it didn't seem like
anyone was there.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.970
Can't get me!

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.200
Wait!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.100
Oh, yeah?! Then I'm going
to have to transform.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.500
Roar! Roar!

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.700
The Prince awoke Sleeping
Beauty and rescued her...

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.780
...and they lived happily
ever after.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.090
Do you want to read
it again, Chibi?

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.920
Chibi?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.000
FILE. 36
THE LOST KITTEN

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.730
I haven't seen Chibi.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.870
Neither have I.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.200
Huh?

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.900
Hello, Ken!

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.880
What's the matter?

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.420
Satoshi!

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.190
Wait for me!

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.220
I brought it, Satoshi!

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.280
Wait!

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.790
I see. You lost
your kitten.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.020
Maybe somebody
stole it!

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.890
Then it's in
trouble.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.130
No! My poor
kitty!

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:33.500
It's okay. Chibi probably just
went off to play, that's all.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:34.800
Think so?

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:35.770
Mmm-hmm.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.840
Then it's lost!

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.980
What do we do?

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:45.110
It's just a kitten, so it couldn't
have gotten very far.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:48.150
How about we all look
for it, together?

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.020
Ow, that hurt.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.490
Where'd that come
from?! Hey!

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.920
That poor little
girl is crying!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.330
You, sir, are an
evil brute!

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.470
Wh... who, me?

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:17.040
Condemn the crime, but pity the criminal!
I shall bring you to justice!

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.950
You deserve to be...

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.650
You're wrong!

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.590
You're wrong!
She lost her kitten!

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.720
Are you serious?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.830
Yeah, Ken said he'd
help me find Chibi.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:53.020
Aah! I almost made
a huge mistake!

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.510
Don't be so hard
on yourself.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.930
Hmm?

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.360
I'm going to help you
find that lost kitty!

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:07.020
Resistance is futile! You
must let me assist you...

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.430
...as compensation for the
injustice I've committed!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.670
You can count
on me!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.070
Can't hurt,
I guess.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.380
Kitty?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.760
How're you making out?

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.560
How're you making out?
Just about done.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.130
Hmm?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:38.060
What perfect timing,
Home Run Girl.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.800
Who are you calling
Home Run Girl?!

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:46.200
Give this to Ken for me, as com-
pensation for an injustice.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.140
What are you talking about?

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.640
What are you talking about?
What?

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:50.700
What are you talking about?

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.040
What's this?!

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.410
There's no need to thank me.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:59.880
To achieve peace on earth, evil must be
wiped out, and justice must prevail!

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:07.790
So tell Ken that I'll definitely find
Chibi! It is my mission in life!

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.420
Hey, wait!

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.760
Aah, he's gone.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.030
He's as nonsensical
as ever.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.140
What should we do
with the kitties?

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.540
We'll just have to take them
back to the station...

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.740
...and try to get in touch
with Nakajima.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.090
So Nakajima and Strike Man
are searching for a cat?

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:37.820
Yeah, I called Nakajima on the
radio, and that's what he said.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.960
What a cutie pie.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.490
The cat they're looking for
isn't one of these, huh?

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:46.150
No. Yoriko, I have
a favor to ask.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:49.330
Can you try and find out
who owns these?

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:50.440
Me?!

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.410
Use your connections! You'll do fine!

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.110
No I won't!

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.040
Sure you will! Good luck!

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.780
Hey, wait!

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.640
What's with the cats?

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:01.820
Detective Tokuno!

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.010
Onto something, Tsujimoto?!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:09.520
Yes, sir! We're investigating the
disappearance of a cat, sir!

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.880
Huh, what a coincidence.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.220
I just happen to be looking
for a cat, myself.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.520
Really, sir?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:21.030
Detective Tokuno, I heard you're
involved in a larceny case.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.840
That's right. I'm looking for a
cat the thieves are hiding.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:28.460
Shall we try to
help you, sir?

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.840
No, this isn't your
ordinary cat.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.000
I won't need
your help.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.150
Yes, sir. Good luck!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.150
Chibi! Chibi! Chibi! Chibi!

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.850
That's strange.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.480
I don't think he's here.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.520
Maybe it went home
to Maho's house.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.560
There's an idea. Maybe it
has a homing instinct.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.030
They said it isn't
at home.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.730
I see.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.810
I guess it's too
young, yet.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.940
Well, I'm glad to have
some help.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.310
What's that thing?

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:07.450
A transmitter.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.010
"Transmitter?"

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.170
Sorry about this, kitty.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.690
Okay, all done.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.650
I'm finished here, too.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.850
Those transmitters will give us an idea
of the size of the cats' territories.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:25.120
You mean it's likely that Chibi
will be in the same area?

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.170
Neat-o!

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.190
That's cool, Miyuki!

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.130
Think you'll find Chibi?

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.240
I'm sure we will.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:35.740
Uncle Ken's going to do his very
best to find your little kitten.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.470
I'll go, too. Let us each
follow one of the cats.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.680
Oh, boy.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:00.160
Oh, no. You
in there?

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.700
Here, Chibi. Chibi?

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:08.100
Ow! Yow, that hurts!
Get off of me! Ow!

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.810
Oh, no!

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.640
Didn't find her.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:22.980
Me either.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.450
What happened to
your face, Ken?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:29.030
What, this? I fought a
cat, and the cat won.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.000
That's pathetic.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.400
That's pathetic.
You're a wussy.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.930
Did it hurt?

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.030
No, I'm fine.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:39.310
Maybe it isn't around
here, after all.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.530
Where in the world
could it be?

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.010
Hey, I just remembered!

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:46.280
What?

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:48.210
Remembered what?

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.250
We still haven't had
our snack today!

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:52.980
Oh, no. You're
right!

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.280
Uh...

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.590
Wow! Look at
all the candy!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:02.520
Okay, everybody gets a reward
for looking for the kitten.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:04.600
Go ahead and choose
something you like.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:05.230
Yay!

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:05.870
Oh, boy!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.460
Yay!
Wahoo! Yippee!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:08.100
All right! Yeah!

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:10.930
All right! Yeah!
I meant the kids.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.530
I want that sponge
candy!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.330
Okay, how many
would you like?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.800
I want some, too!

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.970
Three, please.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:19.630
Three it is. Thank you.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.380
I want some of that, too!

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:23.510
I want some of that, too!
Excuse me, but you're on duty here.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.480
So what? Hey!

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:28.180
Wait, this jumbo pack of
gum looks good, too.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:32.160
You can't get that, Natsumi.
That's a grab bag prize.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.930
Oh, really?

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:35.660
Oh, really?
Try your luck?

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:42.790
Okay! Wonder what I'll get?! I'm a
good girl, so I deserve good luck!

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.400
Yuck, what a drag.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:47.870
You got gipped.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.600
You got gipped.
So much for the good girl.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.870
Give me another
shot at that!

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.710
I want to try, too!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.110
I want to try, too!
Me, too!

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:56.310
Me first!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.680
You're not behaving like a grown-up!

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:58.520
Doesn't matter!

00:10:58.520 --> 00:10:59.540
Women and children first!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.690
She acts like a child.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.310
So. I am a woman!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.590
You want to try the
grab bag, Maho?

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.820
No. I don't want to.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.930
No, I guess you wouldn't want
one of those weird masks.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.580
It's pretty, Maho.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.350
It sure is. You look like a princess.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:33.350
Thank you, Uncle Ken.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:43.420
Yay!

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.120
Hurray!

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.690
Let's start looking for
Maho's kitten again.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.070
It's starting
to get late.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.640
Yeah, it's about time for you
three to get going home.

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:59.110
I'll be able to catch
the cat with this!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.040
No, you'll hurt
him with that!

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.680
No, I won't. This
isn't real.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.320
Yeah. Come on,
let's go get it.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.150
No, you have to
go home now.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.160
Aww...

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.420
That's no fun.

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:15.220
But... But what
about Chibi?

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.990
I'm sure we'll
find her.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.300
But...

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.170
Don't worry.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:31.740
But we looked all over the place.
Is she gone for good?

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.940
I don't think so.

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:36.670
Will I ever see
her again?

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:41.050
If you're this worried about
Chibi, think how she feels.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.120
I'm sure she wants to come
back to you, too.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:47.090
I'm positive.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.320
Mmm-hmm.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.230
Be careful, kids.

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:53.700
Make sure you go straight home, now.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.230
We will!

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.340
Bye!

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:01.800
We'll keep our eye out for
the cat, while on patrol.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.570
Thanks.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.610
We'll give you a call
if we find her.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.750
I'll do the same.
Bye.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.290
What's this?

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.720
Cats, by the
looks of it.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.620
"Strike Man wuz here!"

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:25.930
I don't believe it. He's actually
looking for the missing cat.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:27.790
Seems like it.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.040
Hurry up, Maho!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.510
Maho!

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:41.410
Wait up!

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.040
Wait for me!

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:45.910
There!

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.360
Mine's further!

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.980
Mine's further!
Mine's further!

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.720
A kitty!

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.590
Huh?

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.460
I hear a kitty.

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:58.830
Huh?

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.820
Where?

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.830
See?

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:14.200
I hear a kitty!

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.580
Yeah, so do I!

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.670
I wonder if it's Chibi?

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.250
It's Chibi!

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.690
Chibi!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.600
We found Chibi!

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:35.300
Chibi!

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:38.130
Here, kitty kitty!

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.270
C'mon! Jump up!

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:45.310
Chibi! Chibi!

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:48.370
Look out, Maho!

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.950
Oh, no!
Oh, no!

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:01.050
Maho!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:09.530
Chibi.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.670
Yippee! You got it! You got it!
Yippee! You got it! You got it!

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.910
I'm so happy I found
you, Chibi!

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:24.220
Uh-oh!

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.190
Huh?

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:35.350
"Meow. We're looking
for a lost cat."

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.690
Finished!

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:39.390
That doesn't look anything
like a cat.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:42.300
What do you mean?
It's perfect!

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:46.300
What are you doing, drawing
pictures of raccoons?

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.570
That was uncalled for.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.470
He didn't mean anything by it, it's
just that it doesn't look like a cat.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:53.480
What, that's
a cat?

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:57.850
I take that to mean that you
haven't found your cat.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.110
No, sir. You haven't
either?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.250
No.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.580
Maho's in trouble!

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.180
What?!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.330
What's that? Are
you serious?!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:12.320
Yes, Shou and Yuuta contacted
us from a nearby police box.

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.460
Roger. I'm on
my way.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.970
<i>Damn! This</i>
<i>is terrible!</i>

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.920
Ken.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.220
I'm coming, Maho!

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:17.220
Ken!

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.960
Don't worry, I'll save you! Just
sit down and don't move!

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:24.240
Ken!

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.060
<i>But how am I going</i>
<i>to get to her?!</i>

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.830
Nakajima, there's a bridge
a little ways ahead.

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:30.840
Roger.

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.310
There's a wharf
just beyond it.

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.810
We'll take a boat
from there.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.080
Keep an eye on Maho
'til we get there!

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.910
Roger. I'm counting
on you.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.210
Gotcha.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.090
Ken's coming to
save us, Chibi.

00:17:56.270 --> 00:18:00.000
Hurry up, Tsujimoto! The boat's
going to hit a pylon!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.800
We're at the wharf!
We're on the way!

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.940
Please hurry!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:10.410
Ken!

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:12.110
Sit down!

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:14.310
Sit down, Maho!
Keep down!

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:16.550
Ken!

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:21.590
Oh, no!

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:23.160
Ken!

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.230
I'm coming,
Maho!

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.500
Maho!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:12.970
Nakajima!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:15.110
Maho!

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.080
No way!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:29.900
Nakajima!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.690
Maho!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.660
I'm so happy you found
your kitten, Maho.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.430
And you're
safe now.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.630
Mmm-hmm.

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:45.210
What's the
matter?

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.680
My ring...

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:51.080
My princess ring...
I lost it.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:57.080
I'm sure that one day your true prince
will come and give you another one.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:59.880
My true prince?

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:03.090
Yes. He'll be your
very own prince.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.020
I got it.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:07.670
Huh?

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:09.460
It was floating.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.730
My book!

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.270
Nakajima!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.460
It's soaked, but
it'll be all right.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:20.410
"Sleeping Beauty"

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:25.240
You should have seen Nakajima!
He was so cool!

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.240
Gee, you're pretty impressive
under pressure!

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:30.150
It was nothing.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:33.120
Well, the most important thing
is that Maho wasn't hurt.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:37.030
That reminds me, Detective.
What about your cat?

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:39.630
No leads...

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:40.600
Umm...

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:41.820
Huh?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.660
I completely forgot
about Strike Man.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.000
What's this?

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.800
Is something
the matter?

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:52.040
No doubt about it. This is the
very cat I've been looking for.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:53.370
Really?

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.540
What does a ceramic cat have to
do with a larceny case, anyway?

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:56.980
"senmanyen"

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:59.320
This isn't your average
ceramic cat.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.150
The coin is made
of pure gold.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.880
Wow! Pure
gold!

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:08.550
Those thieves didn't know
what happened to it.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:11.320
This makes
my case.

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:15.060
I wonder if Strike Man will get some
kind of reward for finding it?

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.360
Perhaps.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.560
He's got as much use for a reward
as a cat does for money.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:22.810
He's probably still out
searching for Chibi.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.670
You've got to be kidding!
Not more cats!

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.750
Please!

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.520
I'm gonna win
this time!

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.020
Me, too!

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:36.620
No way!

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.820
Come on,
Maho!

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:41.930
Okay!

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.690
Let's play superheroes!

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:46.800
Okay!

00:21:55.880 --> 00:22:01.380
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:11.990
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.590 --> 00:22:18.930
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:28.970
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:43.020
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:51.200
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:59.040
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:07.880
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:17.450
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:24.930
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:28.300
"There's only one chance."

00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:34.060
The Yamanote line runs from Yokohama,
through Tokyo, and, along with...

00:23:34.170 --> 00:23:39.480
...the Keihin-Tohoku line, starting in Ohmi-
ya, continues to Shinagawa and Tabata.

00:23:39.650 --> 00:23:44.340
A special Keihin-Tohoku line in-train
theft investigation squad is on duty!

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:46.750
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 37...

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:48.720
..."The Yamanote Express Incident."

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:50.720
Hey you two, I'm on my way!
